Hardening patch for the VC-5 decoder of the GoPro GPR SDK
==========================================================

Applies to https://github.com/gopro/gpr at commit
446c736a38fb14f51343605c0780d347dc602f89 (cmake/build-deps.cmake fetches that
commit and applies this file). Only source/lib/vc5_decoder, vc5_common and
common are touched - the directories LibRaw compiles.

THIS IS A MODIFICATION OF GOPRO'S FILES (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)).
Every change is marked in the code with a comment starting "hardening:".

What it does: GoPro's decoder trusts its input; on damaged files it wrote and
read past its buffers. The patch adds bounds and consistency checks that
return an existing CODEC_ERROR code, checks allocation results, and replaces
left shifts of negative values with multiplications (same result). Output on
valid streams is unchanged, except that images whose smallest wavelet band is
under 3x3 pixels (below about 34x34) are now rejected: the inverse transform
read outside its buffers for them.

Original code (C) Copyright 2018 GoPro Inc, Apache License 2.0 or MIT.
Changes made for the undisker LibRaw fork, 2026, under the same terms.

diff --git a/source/lib/vc5_common/bitstream.c b/source/lib/vc5_common/bitstream.c
index cef4312..9617b28 100755
--- a/source/lib/vc5_common/bitstream.c
+++ b/source/lib/vc5_common/bitstream.c
@@ -118,7 +118,13 @@ BITWORD GetBits(BITSTREAM *stream, BITCOUNT count)
         bits = (stream->buffer >> (bit_word_count - count));
         
         // Reduce the number of bits in the bit buffer
-        stream->buffer <<= count;
+        /* hardening: a shift by the full word size is undefined */
+        if (count < bit_word_count) {
+            stream->buffer <<= count;
+        }
+        else {
+            stream->buffer = 0;
+        }
         stream->count = (stream->count - count);
     }
     else
@@ -269,6 +275,16 @@ CODEC_ERROR GetBuffer(BITSTREAM *bitstream)
     // The bit buffer should be empty
     assert(bitstream->count == 0);
     
+    /* hardening: signal an underflow (and supply zero bits) when the memory stream is exhausted */
+    if (bitstream->stream->type == STREAM_TYPE_MEMORY &&
+        bitstream->stream->byte_count >= bitstream->stream->location.memory.size)
+    {
+        bitstream->error = BITSTREAM_ERROR_UNDERFLOW;
+        bitstream->buffer = 0;
+        bitstream->count = bit_word_count;
+        return CodecErrorBitstream(bitstream->error);
+    }
+
     // Fill the bit buffer with a word from the byte stream
     bitstream->buffer = Swap32(GetWord(bitstream->stream));
     bitstream->count = bit_word_count;
